# No automatic pushes

Same constellation rule as monorepo root: **no** `git push` / remote publish unless the user explicitly asks in this turn.

Overnight handoff, SYMBOLS grind, and “continue” mean **local** work only. Leave commits (if requested) on the local branch; wait for an explicit push before touching `origin`.

Submodule bumps on metalpython `wasmmod`/`master` also stay local until the user asks to push.
